# P19 (v203) — পুরোনো বান্ডেল-ক্যাশ-স্টিকিনেস চিরকাল-নিষেধ
# আপডেট-প্রবাহ নিশ্চিত: sw.js ও index.html কখনো HTTP-ক্যাশে আটকাবে না।
# NOTE (v323, owner bug 2026-10-13): the register() call previously used
#   './sw.js?v=<build>'. A versioned JS URL matches the `/*.js?v=*` rule at the
#   bottom of this file (immutable, max-age=31536000), which contradicted this
#   block and pinned an old, broken worker on every device forever — the exact
#   cause of the recurring "This site can't be reached / ERR_FAILED". The
#   registration now uses the bare './sw.js' so ONLY the no-store rule below
#   applies, and every device picks up each new worker on the next load.
# SEC hardening (2026-10-18 audit) — every response, no exceptions.
# HSTS: a first visit over plain http could be stripped to http and hijacked.
# X-Frame-Options + frame-ancestors: the app is never framed (verified: no
#   window.frameElement use, and the dashboard/profile frames use srcdoc, which
#   X-Frame-Options does not apply to), so refusing to be framed costs nothing
#   and closes clickjacking — which mattered most next to the old CORS hole.
# The CSP here is deliberately frame-ancestors ONLY. A full default-src 'self'
#   policy would block the Google fonts, the Datamuse/Dictionary/translate APIs
#   and the inline boot scripts this app relies on, so it needs a browser pass
#   against the live site before it can ship. Do not widen this line blind.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/dashboard-v2.js
